"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkp_vs_np_docs=globalThis.webpackChunkp_vs_np_docs||[]).push([[8097],{65932(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"tag":{"label":"real-world-impact","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/tags/real-world-impact","allTagsPath":"/azeon/p-vs-np/tags","count":12,"items":[{"id":"real-world-impact/airline-crew-scheduling","title":"Airline Crew Scheduling","description":"Every flight needs a legal crew, every crew needs to get home, and the whole plan breaks when a storm hits. Airline crew scheduling is one of the largest NP-Hard problems solved routinely, and it\'s built on set covering.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/airline-crew-scheduling"},{"id":"real-world-impact/circuit-board-design","title":"Circuit Board Design","description":"A modern chip has billions of transistors connected by wires that must all fit, avoid each other and stay short. Splitting, placing and wiring them are NP-Hard problems, solved every day by software most people have never heard of.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/circuit-board-design"},{"id":"real-world-impact/computational-biology","title":"Computational Biology","description":"A protein is a chain that folds itself into a precise 3D shape, and the shape decides what it does. Simplified versions of predicting that shape are NP-Hard. Then, in 2020, AlphaFold started getting real shapes right, and won a Nobel Prize.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/computational-biology"},{"id":"real-world-impact/financial-modeling-and-markets","title":"Financial Modeling & Markets","description":"Spotting an arbitrage loop in currency prices turns out to be easy, which surprised me. Finding the best one isn\'t. And there\'s a serious argument that computational hardness can let sellers hide bad assets inside complex financial products.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/financial-modeling-and-markets"},{"id":"real-world-impact/hash-functions-and-passwords","title":"Hash Functions & Passwords","description":"A good website never knows your password. It stores a fingerprint that\'s easy to compute and believed to be infeasible to reverse. Here\'s how that works, and why the protection isn\'t NP-Hardness, even though it does depend on P \u2260 NP.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/hash-functions-and-passwords"},{"id":"real-world-impact/machine-learning-constraints","title":"Machine Learning Constraints","description":"Training even a tiny neural network perfectly is NP-Hard. Yet machine learning works astonishingly well. The reason is the same lesson again: training never asks for the perfect answer, and real data isn\'t the worst case.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/machine-learning-constraints"},{"id":"real-world-impact/modern-cryptography-rsa","title":"Modern Cryptography (RSA)","description":"How RSA locks a message with a number anyone can see, and why only the person who knows its two prime factors can unlock it. Plus an honest correction: RSA needs much more than P \u2260 NP to be safe.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/modern-cryptography-rsa"},{"id":"real-world-impact/p-vs-np-in-the-boardroom","title":"P vs NP in the Boardroom","description":"Why should someone running a company care about a math problem? Because the moment a product promises the \'best\' schedule, route or match, it has probably walked into NP-Hard territory, and the way you handle that is a business decision.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/p-vs-np-in-the-boardroom"},{"id":"real-world-impact/resource-allocation-in-saas","title":"Resource Allocation in SaaS","description":"Every cloud app runs on servers, and someone has to decide which job goes on which machine. Use too many machines and you waste money; pack too tightly and things crash. Underneath is bin packing, and it\'s NP-Hard.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/resource-allocation-in-saas"},{"id":"real-world-impact/social-media-graph-algorithms","title":"Social Media Graph Algorithms","description":"A social network is a graph with billions of nodes. Finding the largest group where everyone knows everyone is the Clique problem from Post 15, NP-Hard and even hard to approximate. So platforms quietly ask easier questions instead.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/social-media-graph-algorithms"},{"id":"real-world-impact/supply-chain-logistics","title":"Supply Chain Logistics","description":"Every parcel van starts the morning with a Traveling Salesman Problem plus extra rules. Companies can\'t solve it perfectly, so they solve it well, and the gap between \'good\' and \'best\' is measured in millions of kilometres.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/supply-chain-logistics"},{"id":"real-world-impact/the-cost-of-inefficiency","title":"The Cost of Inefficiency","description":"How much money does the world lose because we can\'t solve NP-Hard problems perfectly? I went looking for the number. Nobody can honestly calculate it, and the reason is itself a lesson about NP-Hardness.","permalink":"/azeon/p-vs-np/real-world-impact/the-cost-of-inefficiency"}],"unlisted":false}}')}}]);